    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "10001",
          "body": "**Starting Stage 1 development** alongside [ROKJ-3](https://satsumya.atlassian.net/browse/ROKJ-3).\n\nBuilding member profile setup flow from acceptance criteria: location, difficulty levels (default colour sequence), optional fields, pet rock avatar placeholders, then dashboard.\n\nWill mark criteria complete on this ticket as each item is implemented in the clickable prototype.",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:01:32.346+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:01:32.346+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10004",
          "body": "**Implementation complete — ready for review**\n\nAll acceptance criteria marked complete in member profile setup screen (`/profile/setup`).\n\n**Test paths:**\n\n1. Happy path: complete all fields including optional username/strengths\n2. Alternate path: skip optional fields, still complete with required location\n3. Error path: tap Complete profile without adding a location\n\nLinked from sign up welcome flow ([ROKJ-3](https://satsumya.atlassian.net/browse/ROKJ-3)).",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:06:11.575+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:06:11.575+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10006",
          "body": "Added prototype test links to the ticket description, populated the **Decision tree**, and reformatted **Outcome summary** as bullets + scenario table.\n\nProfile scenarios are also available from http://localhost:8081/scenarios (run `npm run web` first).",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:15:16.903+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:15:16.903+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10010",
          "body": "Moved to the ticket fields",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:52:11.094+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:52:11.094+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10012",
          "body": "Review: <custom data-type=\"status\" data-id=\"id-0\">not approved</custom> \n\nPlease address the following:\n\n|  | **Summary** | **Description** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Required and optional field communication | Use an \\* for required fields and don’t mention optional as that is already implied |\n| 2 | Input errors | Error validation should happen in real time instead of waiting until the user tries to continue |\n| 3 | Remove excess prototype text | Some text on this ticket was added for context but not needed on the prototype e.g. “Default option: cartoon pet rocks” Please remove any text that a user wouldn’t expect to see |\n| 4 | Need to be able to exit member profile | Some fields are required for users to use other features but users can still exit the member profile set up if they want to |\n| 5 | Username needs validation | We’ll need to check if a username is available. For testing please make ‘thegoat’ a username that’s already taken so we can view that scenario |\n| 6 | 'Location name' / location | This field should be an address search with suggested addresses showing as the user types. If the user enters a location and the address can’t be found, there should be an option to add anyway  |\n| 7 | Location added - encourage user to add levels | When a location is added it needs to feel more seamless to move users onto adding difficulty levels |\n| 8 | Location edit | After a location is added a user needs to be able to edit the location easily if they made a mistake or need to update the location |\n| 9 | Difficulty levels sort | Make it clear they are adding level from easy to hard and allow users to swap the sorting from hard to easy |\n| 10 | Remove level numbers | e.g. Level 1 name should just be “Level label” |\n| 11 | Changing level colours | Allow users to click on the colour to open a menu or dropdown of the default colour types or click a plus button to choose from a colour wheel with hex code available |\n| 12 | Difficulty levels - removing | If a user adds too many difficulty levels they need to be able to remove a level if they want. But a user should not be able to delete the level if there’s no other levels added to the location |\n| 13 | Be concise when displaying levels | Try showing levels as a row so it’s less overwhelming and easier for users to see more levels |\n| 14 | Difficulty level rearranging | Users should also be able to drag the levels to a different position as well as moving with arrows |\n| 15 | Locations added | Only show one location with levels at a time. e.g. an accordion for each location, only allow one location accordion open at any time |\n| 16 | Home location communication | Use a symbol to show which location is the home/base instead of saying ‘home/base’ |\n| 17 | Change home location | Users need to be able to change which location is considered the ‘home’ |\n| 18 | Remove excess level summary text | “Current levels: Yellow (#F5D547), Blue (#4A90D9), Purple (#9B59B6), Green (#2ECC71), Orange (#E67E22), Red (#E74C3C), Black (#2C3E50), White (#ECF0F1), Pink (#FF69B4), Custom (#AAAAAA), Custom (#AAAAAA), Custom (#AAAAAA)“  \nit only seems to provide a summary of the first location added not all locations added and doesn’t add any extra value |\n| 19 | Level colour cannot be blank | don’t allow users to remove a colour without adding a colour |\n| 20 | Strength and areas to improve | These should add tags so it’s clear when it’s been added. These tags should be able to be removed as well. Offer some recommended tags that a user can tap to add, typing should be secondary |\n\nGeneral feedback: please use the existing ticket fields where possible e.g. decision tree and outcome summary. I’ve moved these from comments to the ticket fields",
          "created": "2026-06-20T15:18:29.493+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T16:03:42.657+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        }
      ],
